Build mln-rs-c with any one backend's feature.

Every native build had to enable all of mln-rs-c's backend features: its
code named Vulkan's, OpenGL's and WebGPU's types and constructors under
platform cfgs alone, so `--no-default-features --features vulkan` failed
on the OpenGL arms, and `--features gl` on the Vulkan ones. The supported
backend mask and the OpenGL provider mask listed every backend of the
platform, too, so a host couldn't tell which one a build is for.

build.rs now sets `backend_vulkan` and `backend_gl`, each a backend's
feature on a platform that has the backend, and the C API's Vulkan and
OpenGL code, the backend list, and the provider mask take those cfgs.
Native WebGPU follows its feature. mln_vulkan becomes optional under the
`vulkan` feature, as mln_gl is under `gl`. With `backend_gl` covering
Windows, custom layers also see WGL's encoders and passes, which only EGL
builds got before.

It also carries include/maplibre_native_c/gpu_device.h's account of which
devices take an adapter: only Vulkan takes `adapter_uuid` or
`adapter_luid`, and OpenGL takes none.

Upstream as louwers/mln-rs#323; drop this patch once the pin includes it.

